\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Horizons beyond the exterior model
\citet{Section 3.2.4, Theorem 3.3, pp. 59--60}{meinrenken2013clifford};
\citet{Section 2.4, Theorem 8, pp. 286--287}{kostant1997clifford};
\citet{I.2, pp. 13--19}{lawson2016spin}}

\p{The exterior model now has two distinct faithful-range results. In even
split dimension, \ref{fcap-002V} constructs all matrix units, identifies the
two even endomorphism blocks, and records irreducibility after restriction to
Spin under its separably closed, positive-rank hypotheses. In odd complex
dimension, \ref{fcap-002W} shows that either full Clifford action selects one
simple summand, while its restriction to the even algebra is faithful and its
actual Spin action exchanges exterior parity in positive rank. Thus exterior
parity is not a decomposition into odd-dimensional Spin submodules.}

\p{The occupation lines of \ref{fcap-0025} have also been joined to root and
highest-weight theory. The type-D calculation in \ref{fcap-002X} and
\ref{fcap-002Y} fixes a Borel, proves positive-nilradical generation, and
identifies the two fork modules. The type-B calculation in
\ref{fcap-002Z} adds the short root and its irreducible spin module, while
\ref{fcap-0030} derives the finite type-B and type-D characters on the
actual Spin torus. The selected TauCeti declarations formalize the Clifford
root actions, annihilation identities, and weight vectors. The complex Borel,
scalar-extension, irreducibility, torus-descent, and character conclusions
are the mathematical arguments in these notes, not one packaged formal
theorem.}

\p{The generic differential of a smooth group homomorphism remains separate
in \ref{fcap-001Q}--\ref{fcap-001W}: the selected formal interface does not
yet identify the differential of the concrete Spin vector action with the
quadratic Clifford lift. Further low-dimensional module comparisons and
triality likewise require their own group maps and convention checks. The
real Bott-periodic algebra table in \ref{fcap-0016} and its
signature-#{(1,3)} instance in \ref{fcap-0026} do not supply those missing
representation-theoretic or differential bridges.}
